From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: reject GL initialization without context callbacks (STEAMAC-61)

A flags override can request vrend from a Venus-only client. The context
wrapper calls NULL callbacks when no internal winsys exists. Reject the
unsupported combination before entering vrend; keep proper GL clients intact.

diff --git a/src/virglrenderer.c b/src/virglrenderer.c
--- a/src/virglrenderer.c
+++ b/src/virglrenderer.c
@@ -1022,6 +1022,16 @@
          goto fail;
       }
 
+      /* Without an internal winsys these wrappers call the client's GL
+       * callbacks directly. Venus-only clients may leave all three NULL. */
+      if (!state.winsys_initialized && !state.external_winsys_initialized &&
+          (!cbs->create_gl_context || !cbs->destroy_gl_context || !cbs->make_current)) {
+         virgl_error("OpenGL renderer requested without GL context callbacks "
+                     "(flags 0x%x); Venus-only clients must set NO_VIRGL\n", flags);
+         ret = -EINVAL;
+         goto fail;
+      }
+
       /* vrend's sync thread requires a real eventfd (it creates one
        * internally); without one, keep vrend on the poll path -- the pipe
        * fallback above is scoped to the proxy. */
